  "notes": [
    "Sources: pinned stan/multi_occupancy.stan and models/posteriordb_multi_occupancy_butterfly.py::build_model.",
    "Map correlation_unit=(rho_uv+1)/2 and uv=column_stack(uv1,uv2), retaining all S species, including S-n never-observed species. The PyMC Cholesky factor induces the same covariance with diagonals sigma_uv**2 and off-diagonal sigma_uv[0]*sigma_uv[1]*rho_uv. Stan already evaluates Beta(2,2) at (rho_uv+1)/2 without a Jacobian; its value equals PyMC's Beta density at correlation_unit. The coordinate determinant |d rho_uv/d correlation_unit|=2 is constant (log(2)); normalizing Stan's rho prior removes the same constant. The two positive Cauchy-to-HalfCauchy normalizations add only 2*log(2) to raw PyMC logp. Observed and never-observed inclusion/occupancy mixtures match, including the J-fold zero-site likelihood for each never-observed species; no latent species are discarded.",
    "No nonconstant density adjustment is required by these source definitions; parameter-independent constants are omitted from two-point deltas."
  ],
